{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets","id":487101,"title":"Resources cost for Silver Bullets?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-21T02:15:29-07:00","id":487101,"title":"Resources cost for Silver Bullets?","content":"Yep, it's reached a point where my players have started asking, bless their wicked hearts.<br /> <br /> Browsed Armory and couldn't find it.<br /> <br /> So what's the Resources price for one clip per player/squad(4-5 people)/platoon(15-30 people)?<br /> <br /> Yes, platoon, they have big plans. Yes, I'm going to allow it. Yes, the campaign is going swell, fantastic even, thanks for asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T02:46:14-07:00","id":487133,"title":"","content":"Whatever the materials cost, I would increase the required availability dots due to scarcity. It's not like you can walk into your local Walmart or Cabelas and buy silver bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T03:14:28-07:00","id":487139,"title":"","content":"Yeah, raw silver and a bit of craft skill is probably the way to go. Any of your pcs know metalwork?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T03:17:49-07:00","id":487140,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://silverbulletbullion.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Actually</a>, <a href=\"http://www.jmbullion.com/silver/silver-bullets/\" target=\"_blank\">you</a> <a href=\"http://www.providentmetals.com/bullion/silver/private-slv/silver-bullets.html\" target=\"_blank\">can</a>.<br /> <br /> But since we're looking $20 to $50 per bullet, well, a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T03:25:19-07:00","id":487142,"title":"","content":"Silver is also a comparatively <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_bullet\" target=\"_blank\">crappy metal for actual bullets and blades</a>.<br /> <br /> If you're going the silver ammunition route, choose a nice reliable shotgun and silver slugs or 00 buckshot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T03:25:35-07:00","id":487143,"title":"","content":"I don't think those are real bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T03:47:51-07:00","id":487150,"title":"","content":"Lies! Lies and heresy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T08:49:35-07:00","id":488327,"title":"","content":"Home smithing kit: ~65 dollars<br /> 3 ounces of silver: ~80 dollars<br /> 9mm mold: ~40 dollars<br /> Butane torch: ~50 dollars<br /> Loading press: ~150 dollars<br /> <br /> A clip of werewolf killers? Priceless.<br /> <br /> Naturally you need the base supplies too, powder, casings, etc, and a few hours of personal time but that's really it. In fact, most gun enthusiasts would already have all the basic materials requires, minus the silver itself.<br /> <br /> So if you know somebody who has the above supplies you could get silver bullets for Resources 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> To answer the question giving 30 guys a single clip of silver depends on what kind of guns they use. 30 guys with 9mm handguns would cost <b>$3000</b> in raw silver, before any labor or supply costs. Automatic rifles would cost about the same due to less metal per bullet. These are purely based on weight, mind you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","user":"Full Time GM","date":". 04-22-2015, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T09:39:22-07:00","id":488376,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the repair costs on the weapons actually firing those bullets, as the bullets already deform pretty badly in the gun, leaving molten silver behind and possibly damaging it.<br /> <br /> Just use a shotgun with silver buckshot. Far easier to make and maintain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T09:47:34-07:00","id":488386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488376#post488376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the repair costs on the weapons actually firing those bullets, as the bullets already deform pretty badly in the gun, leaving molten silver behind and possibly damaging it.<br /> <br /> Just use a shotgun with silver buckshot. Far easier to make and maintain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would silver slugs be very different than buckshot? I've had a handful of wolf-blooded NPCs in my game carry around 2-5 slugs since I figured making a slug was easier than buckshot. I could be wrong. Despite being from Texas I know virtually nothing about guns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T09:59:30-07:00","id":488394,"title":"","content":"I find it hard to imagine someone actually using silver bullets against werewolves enough that they'd be able to go repair the damage it does. A human with silver bullets is going to be a seriously fragile glass cannon. Werewolves have tremendous speed and deadly weapons, my own character has a dicepool of 3 for brawl attacks in human form and can still kill an average human in one shot with one of the more combat-worthy forms. And disarming is just a matter of Strength and Brawl contested by the opponent's Strength and Athletics. Considering how many of the forms add to Strength you might have a huge advantage there.<br /> <br /> Plus, the urshul form can cause arm wrack on a target once per scene when they damage them. The first line of arm wrack states that the victim drops whatever they're holding with that arm.<br /> <br /> Still, just to be careful my own character was pondering taking over one of the Cash for Gold businesses and making fair offers for silver, which would promptly be ruined.<br /> <br /> Overall, I don't think having plain silver bullets would require any more resources than regular bullets. But if you were doing it long term, an actual werewolf hunter repairing guns and so forth, maybe another dot to justify the new guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-22-2015, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:06:39-07:00","id":488419,"title":"","content":"I think anyone making silver bullets would end up in one of two situations:<br /> <br /> 1. They plan ahead and have the element of surprise. In that case, there's likely going to be more than one of them, and it's going to be an ambush. The werewolf would almost certainly go down, even if they managed to take someone with them.<br /> <br /> 2. They are caught by surprise, in which case they have the silver bullets as a protection. Odds really aren't with them on this one. They might get a lucky shot and survive, though, which is infinitely better than the state of &quot;You are now Uratha dung&quot; that every other option provides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:20:24-07:00","id":488712,"title":"","content":"7 replies and still no mention of how many Resources Dots it would cost an individual/squad/platoon!<br /> <br /> Well done guys!<br /> <br /> Don't worry, I'll extrapolate based on the prices listed here!<br /> <br /> So thanks anyways!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T15:05:48-07:00","id":488743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488712#post488712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7 replies and still no mention of how many Resources Dots it would cost an individual/squad/platoon!<br /> <br /> Well done guys!<br /> <br /> Don't worry, I'll extrapolate based on the prices listed here!<br /> <br /> So thanks anyways!</div> </div> </div> </div>Individual 1, Squad 2, Platoon 3 or 4. That's for basic pistols and revolvers, I would go up one for something special like rifles, but not above 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-22-2015, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T15:39:56-07:00","id":488792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488712#post488712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7 replies and still no mention of how many Resources Dots it would cost an individual/squad/platoon!<br /> <br /> Well done guys!<br /> <br /> Don't worry, I'll extrapolate based on the prices listed here!<br /> <br /> So thanks anyways!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the point is that Resources alone may be insufficient to obtain silver ammunition, or that additional merits or skills may be required, such as a few dots in Crafts to make the ammunition on your own (and maintain the firearms ruined by the silver), or Contacts, Retainer or Allies (or Fixer, Esoteric Armory, etc.) for them to make or procure it for you. The cost and availability of silver ammunition exceeds the cost of just the silver due to its scarcity in <i>your</i> nWOD. Silver purchases and sales, capable gunsmiths, etc. may also be watched carefully by werewolves and their spirit and mundane spies and allies. After you procure the silver ammunition, it's entirely possible that characters may also promptly get a visit from local law enforcement, Homeland Security, mental health professionals, Task Force: Valkyrie, etc. <br /> <br /> Outfitting a platoon or other large group with regular sources of esoteric, no less relatively expensive, ammunition such as silver, may be the province of governments and large corporations (and Mages with Matter), and outside the purview of PC's without a <i>very</i> good explanation.<br /> <br /> Dots in Resources alone should not be able to solve all your more unusual procurement needs. It is not always a stand-in for other Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:34:21-07:00","id":488865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488792#post488792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think the point is that Resources alone may be insufficient to obtain silver ammunition, or that additional merits or skills may be required, such as a few dots in Crafts to make the ammunition on your own (and maintain the firearms ruined by the silver), or Contacts, Retainer or Allies (or Fixer, Esoteric Armory, etc.) for them to make or procure it for you. The cost and availability of silver ammunition exceeds the cost of just the silver due to its scarcity in <i>your</i> nWOD. Silver purchases and sales, capable gunsmiths, etc. may also be watched carefully by werewolves and their spirit and mundane spies and allies. After you procure the silver ammunition, it's entirely possible that characters may also promptly get a visit from local law enforcement, Homeland Security, mental health professionals, Task Force: Valkyrie, etc.<br /> <br /> Outfitting a platoon or other large group with regular sources of esoteric, no less relatively expensive, ammunition such as silver, may be the province of governments and large corporations (and Mages with Matter), and outside the purview of PC's without a <i>very</i> good explanation.<br /> <br /> Dots in Resources alone should not be able to solve all your more unusual procurement needs. It is not always a stand-in for other Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to this, yes, you could likely purchase a cheap box of &quot;silver&quot; ammo online. 90% of the time it'd be useless, or would completely ruin your firearm after the first shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:39:29-07:00","id":488873,"title":"","content":"I feel like this provides a good reference point on what being attacked by a werewolf is like:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/personal-experiences-1584-6-things-you-learn-being-mauled-by-bears.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cracked.com/personal-expe...-by-bears.html</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:46:48-07:00","id":488879,"title":"","content":"Armory p88 says you have to make your own ammo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:10:13-07:00","id":488900,"title":"","content":"You can just buy silver coins or silverware at a pawn shop and melt it down, people make their own bullets on the cheap pretty easily as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:10:20-07:00","id":488974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488900#post488900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can just buy silver coins or silverware at a pawn shop and melt it down, people make their own bullets on the cheap pretty easily as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember that according to W:tF 2e, p. 101, silver weapons and ammunition must be at least 80% pure to gain the intended benefit against werewolves. Many of the silver coins that may be readily available, such as Kennedy half-dollars, are far below this threshold (usually only about 20-40% silver). Older, ~80% silver coins are much more expensive, rare, and their purchase easily traceable. Shooting a werewolf with &quot;cheap&quot; or impure silver will just get him angrier, and is <i>not </i>recommended! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Although normal bullets are relatively easy to make, it still requires Crafts and related skills and/or Merits besides Resources, either to manufacture yourself, or find someone to do it for you, which has its own complications and risks. Additionally, silver is a lousy metal for bullets, and hence requires better than average gunsmithing skills. Gun jams and exploding barrels are quick means of become werewolf kibble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:15:21-07:00","id":488976,"title":"","content":"Since 1986, America has been minting the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Silver_Eagle\" target=\"_blank\">American Silver Eagle</a> coin, which is 99.9% silver. And considering there's over 300 million of them in circulation they're probably not that hard to find. Providing you're playing in modern times, a simple websearch can find that or a comparable material. You could even just just buy raw silver bars.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, yes you'll need crafts to make said bullets, but that's a small investment and many bullet making kits and machines would probably give you bonuses to crafting them. Silver bullets aren't likely to cause problems outside of long term use, but at this point you're really micromanaging something that should be glossed over in story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-22-2015, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:19:30-07:00","id":488978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488873#post488873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this provides a good reference point on what being attacked by a werewolf is like:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/personal-experiences-1584-6-things-you-learn-being-mauled-by-bears.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cracked.com/personal-expe...-by-bears.html</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting, but don't forget that werewolves are also much smarter that your <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1pqyax6gwzQ\" target=\"_blank\">average bear</a>, work in packs, and have supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> Believing that silver alone will solve your pesky werewolf problem is usually a terminal mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:24:58-07:00","id":488979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488978#post488978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Believing that silver alone will solve your pesky werewolf problem is usually a terminal mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But iamthenight wasn't asking about a werewolf problem, they were asking about how to get silver bullets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:34:43-07:00","id":488984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488712#post488712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7 replies and still no mention of how many Resources Dots it would cost an individual/squad/platoon!<br /> <br /> Well done guys!</div> </div> </div> </div>Pity help me, I laughed up a lung at this.<br /> <br /> If your characters can access DIY bullet-making, nofather has it right; buying up the silver, melting it down, and preparing it would be Resources 1 for a few rounds for one person, Resources 2 for a few for a small group of people. To equip a larger group, of about two dozen, you're looking at Resouces 5.<br /> <br /> If your characters <i>lack</i> access to such equipment, they're out of luck unless they have the exact right contacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:35:54-07:00","id":488985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488976#post488976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since 1986, America has been minting the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Silver_Eagle\" target=\"_blank\">American Silver Eagle</a> coin, which is 99.9% silver. And considering there's over 300 million of them in circulation they're probably not that hard to find. Providing you're playing in modern times, a simple websearch can find that or a comparable material. You could even just just buy raw silver bars.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, yes you'll need crafts to make said bullets, but that's a small investment and many bullet making kits and machines would probably give you bonuses to crafting them. Silver bullets aren't likely to cause problems outside of long term use, but at this point you're really micromanaging something that should be glossed over in story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would procurement of expensive and unusual ammunition necessarily be &quot;glossed over in the story?&quot; To do so is certainly a viable choice by a group or ST, but it could just as easily be an important part of the chronicle. What you consider &quot;micromanaging,&quot; others may consider realism or drama, particularly if the story takes place in certain, usually urban, regions and/or where guns and gunsmithing skills and equipment, are rare. Besides, it's not like anyone is demanding that the OP actually spend hours role-playing the purchase of silver or gunsmithing of the bullets.<br /> <br /> In any event, the OP inquired what level of Resources would be required to purchase silver bullets. We both appear to agree that Resources alone would likely be insufficient, and our dispute is really little more some bickering about what other skills and merits would be required and whether it would be good for the OP's chronicle, the latter of which we have no substantive information..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:49:55-07:00","id":489000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488985#post488985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would procurement of expensive and unusual ammunition necessarily be &quot;glossed over in the story?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because we've established that it's not that expensive, as you can buy a silver bar for the cost of the Werewolf the Forsaken second edition core rules. And not even that unusual, since you can just buy already made silver bullets online as Allan53 pointed out or just walk over to a gun shop and get a bullet making kit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T23:53:04-07:00","id":489119,"title":"","content":"Everyone keeps saying that silver bullets will destroy your gun or melt in the barrel or explode or be less effective. <br /> <br /> But the previously linked Wikipedia article states none of that. Silver has a higher melting point than bronze, which was a common material. It's harder than bronze. <br /> <br /> The article even mentions that silver bullets are probably more effective at close range than lead, with their effectiveness dropping for longer ranges. <br /> <br /> @BigDamnHero: a shotgun would have buckshot in a plastic cartridge which would protect the gun from the horrifically corrosive silver . Iirc, said shell breaks apart as the shot leaves the barrel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T01:00:53-07:00","id":489141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=488879#post488879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Armory p88 says you have to make your own ammo.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good catch.<br /> <br /> Although Armory doesn't indicate a price for silver weapons, it does state the following under 1e mechanics [pp. 19, 88-89, 163-64]:<br /> <br /> ****[MODS: If I quoted too much text from the book, kindly delete. Thank you]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Silver<br /> Silver is a soft metal. Blades made of silver are<br /> less effective than those of steel. Because of this, silver<br /> weapons inflict a \u20131 modifier to attack, and only have a<br /> Durability 2, as opposed to steel, which has a Durability of<br /> 3 or more. Of course, silver weapons are of particular use<br /> against Lupines. The metal burns their flesh as the silver<br /> injures, doing far greater damage than it perhaps should.<br /> This damage is aggravated, and does not heal with the<br /> speed to which werewolves are normally accustomed. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But What About . . . ?<br /> Thanks to popular entertainment and dedicated<br /> monster-hunters, many nonstandard ammunition types<br /> are available to enterprising characters. None of the<br /> following ammo is commercially available. Characters<br /> must load their own using the reloading rules on p. 164.<br /> An innately armor-piercing caliber loses this effect with<br /> any of the following custom ammunition types.<br /> <br /> * * *<br /> <br /> Silver: The traditional cure for werewolf problems is a<br /> silver bullet. Silver and lead are slightly different in density,<br /> so a silver bullet is weighted roughly the same as an FMJ<br /> round. Silver is a softer metal than copper, though, which<br /> means that a silver bullet will leave a lot of itself on the<br /> inside of the barrel and will deform more from the initial<br /> stress of firing.<br /> Mechanics: Silver ammunition suffers a \u20131 penalty to<br /> its Damage rating. </div> </div> </div>The remaining relevant sections of in the book deal detail equipment such as Gunsmithing Kits and Reloading Benches, as well as rules rules for Reloading Bullets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T07:40:05-07:00","id":489451,"title":"","content":"I actually did some research on this subject for a novel I wrote and am in the process of attempting to publish. Asking the proprietors of a local gunstore about silver bullets, the only thing they could really come up with is that, because silver is a little bit harder than lead, it might cause the gun barrel to deteriorate a little bit more quickly, to the point of having to replace the barrel after firing 1,000 rounds, instead of 10,000 as with &quot;normal&quot; ammo. Proper maintenance and cleaning will, of course, extend the barrel life of any gun.<br /> <br /> As for actual Resources costs, I would say that functional silver ammo just doesn't exist. It's too expensive and not worth it. Any silver ammo will be hand-crafted, or produced on small-scale for those who find they require it fairly often (like better-funded Hunter groups.) If the PCs can make a contact that supplies them with ready-made silver bullets, add a dot or two to the normal ammo cost for a given gun. Otherwise, they have to obtain silver (use current price guidelines to establish how much silver they can buy with a given amount of Resources funds), and then roll Crafts to make decent bullets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T09:56:45-07:00","id":490646,"title":"","content":"Once you've invested in the required tools (resources 2) I would rule you only need resources 1 to get the silver required to make ammo yourself, resources 2 if you were having it made by a gunsmith and you supply the silver. Silver ingots are cheap and easy to come by, I have a couple at home right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-24-2015, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T10:00:19-07:00","id":490648,"title":"","content":"That should say &quot;and only resources 2 if you supply the silver&quot;, phone browser won't let me edit properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:32:05-07:00","id":490749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=490648#post490648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That should say &amp;quot;and only resources 2 if you supply the silver&amp;quot;, phone browser won't let me edit properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed it for ya.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T01:08:59-07:00","id":494513,"title":"","content":"you can easily make primitive grenades that disperse silver shrapnel. Maybe mix silver with magnesium to produce something like an irritant gas? And of course shooting werewolf's human/wolf form in the head would kill him without any silver. probably also invest some money into industrial flamethrower. They require no permit and shoot up to 50ft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:32:47-07:00","id":494857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=494513#post494513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe mix silver with magnesium to produce something like an irritant gas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the new rules state clearly that silver has to be in mostly pure form to harm werewolves, not alloyed or in solution (as the oft-misused &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_nitrate\" target=\"_blank\">silver nitrate.</a>&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:05:37-08:00","id":800814,"title":"","content":"I often thought that Silver bullets would be much more available in the World of Darkness than in our world, simply because, there is an actual use of them. The main law of Demand and Supply in Economics states that, the higher the demand, the more supply there will be. Since Werewolves are one of the more numerous species in the New World of Darkness (about half a million in the first printing), how can there <i>NOT</i> be a market for silver bullets?<br /> <br /> In the &quot;real world&quot; there are tons of people who have written articles about making silver bullets. You can even buy silver bullet shaped bullion on the market if you are into that kind of thing (it does not fire out of a gun but is a cool investment). If people discuss it on the internet on guns and ammo forums you will see some people joke about a &quot;werewolf problem&quot;. However, in the World of Darkness this would not be a joke and a serious concern, so there would most likely be an underground, or even over the counter market for silver bullets. Since Werewolves are in most parts of the world, it would pay to have some silver bullets just in case. <br /> <br /> Hunters cells, compacts, and conspiracies tend to be internet savvy and well connected. Surely there would be a way to transfer resources among hunters, and some hunter cells would know another hunter cell that happens to have Silver bullets that they can send over. Since casting bullets can be done at home and silver is not too expensive, there must be tons of basement industries devoted to the manufacture and distribution and sale of Silver bullets. <br /> <br /> What Vampire Prince does not keep a supply of Silver bullets or blades on hand just in case? I really liked the scenario in &quot;Under a Blood Red Moon&quot; which depicted a pretty good conflict between Vampires and Werewolves. Basically, Vampires would supply their ghouls with silver bullets and have them fight werewolves. The same template can be used in the new World of Darkness too. Some vampire in the city would have a ghoul in a basement manufacturing some special bullets &quot;just in case...&quot;. <br /> <br /> Some humans would probably start some industries simply to meet demand. If suddenly strange people are asking about silver bullets that can be shot out of a gun (or shotguns with silver shot), then someone would start making them simply to fill a need. These people don't even need to know that werewolves exist but would only be reacting to a market demand and fill that demand to generate a profit. <br /> <br /> Of course, the werewolves in the world would probably be trying to shut down such operations, but there is probably no way that they could completely silence the market. If your territory is in Idaho and the local hunters are buying their silver bullets from some guy in Brazil, it would be tricky to shut the supplier down. <br /> <br /> Then you need to consider a well funded Hunter group like Task Force VALKYRIE. These guys are funded by the US army and so probably have a huge budget to buy all the silver weapons that they need. They are also a task force which probably gets support from other branches of the military. If they need a company of Marines to shoot shiny bullets against hairy insurgents, I am sure that they can arrange it. Sure silver bullets might cost $20.00 each, considering the silver content, but when the US military budget is $600 Billion, it would not take long to make enough to keep the local werewolf problem under control.<br /> <br /> In addition, Task Force Valkyrie would probably lobby the government to allow the sale of Silver Bullets among ammo shops around the country. After all, why should they do all the hunting? By flooding the market with silver bullets they would allow any aspiring hunter cell the weapons they need to eliminate any local packs. That would keep the werewolf population in check and allow Task Force Valkyrie to focus their efforts on the most dangerous packs. <br /> <br /> Mages would probably be able to <i>make their own silver </i>through magik so making silver bullets would be a joke to them. Surely some would capitalize on this to corner the market. <br /> <br /> So yea...I believe that the channels to obtain silver weapons would be available if there was a demand. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:28:54-08:00","id":800838,"title":"","content":"Holy Thread Necromancy, Batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T04:33:40-08:00","id":822259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487101-resources-cost-for-silver-bullets?p=487140#post487140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://silverbulletbullion.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Actually</a>, <a href=\"http://www.jmbullion.com/silver/silver-bullets/\" target=\"_blank\">you</a> <a href=\"http://www.providentmetals.com/bullion/silver/private-slv/silver-bullets.html\" target=\"_blank\">can</a>.<br /> <br /> But since we're looking $20 to $50 per bullet, well, a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't really bullets, those are replica's made entirely of silver and are probably solid silver. A silver bullet doesn't also need a silver casing.<br /> <br /> EDIT; After a bit of research, a standard .308 round cast from silver would be worth around 14 dollars worth of silver, discounting the cost of the powder and the casing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":9807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","user":"Blue-01.exe","date":". 02-03-2016, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T07:42:49-08:00","id":822371,"title":"","content":"In Hunter the Vigil: Spirit Slayers it states that Silver Weaponry increases the cost by one per size category/10 bullets, so you might want to go with that.<br /> Page 143, if anybody's curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T21:30:02-08:00","id":823058,"title":"","content":"5000,000 per 7 billion humans isn't exactly a high population percentage, and the fact that werewolves actually exist isn't going to be common knowledge, especially when those werewolves hunt down and eliminate outsiders to preserve their secrets. Start requesting your local gunsmith if they can make up silver bullets for you and you should start hoping really hard that they aren't wolf blooded or werewolves themselves, assuming you even know there is such thing as wolf blooded. That's how there isn't a market for them. People still get put in jail or institutions for shooting strangers and saying they were justified because those strangers were inhuman monsters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:com